R"VG(
# watermark.vg (Z-06): a made species' watermark, the words a futuristic or far-future people wrote into the genome of a life it made (as
# JCVI-syn1.0's genome carried its makers' names and three sayings: Gibson et al. 2010). Written outside the catalogue at the year it was
# made (`writeWatermark`, peoples/genres.cpp), its maker the writer cast where it was made, the species' facts beside the record's
# (`madeway` light, chemical, dead, grazer or predator; `madeplace` water, soil, rock, ice, salt or spring; `madeglow`); read on the ship's
# decoder in the people's tongue. Rules `wm.`; what it was made for and the far future's own in watermark_far.vg (`wm.for`, `wm.ff.`).
# Every word apart, so no people's records move; every long sentence composed of parts (the records' measure: 5% at a hundred).
@apart
@root watermark

watermark (words=22..150)
  (age=futuristic has:writer 3) {@cast writer}{wm.head}\n{wm.what} {wm.made}\n{wm.for}\n{wm.say}\n{wm.end}
  (age=futuristic has:writer 3) {@cast writer}{wm.head}\n{wm.made} {wm.for}\n{wm.what}\n{wm.reader}\n{wm.end}
  (age=futuristic has:writer 2) {@cast writer}{wm.head}\n{wm.for} {wm.made}\n{wm.say} {wm.reader}
  (age=futuristic !has:writer) {wm.head}\n{wm.what} {wm.for}\n{wm.say}\n{wm.reader}\n{wm.end}
  (age=farfuture 2) {wm.ff.head}\n{wm.ff.what} {wm.for}\n{wm.ff.say}\n{wm.ff.end}
  (age=farfuture 2) {wm.ff.head}\n{wm.for}\n{wm.ff.what} {wm.ff.reader}\n{wm.ff.end}
  (age=farfuture has:writer 2) {@cast writer}{wm.ff.head}\n{wm.ff.what} {wm.ff.signed}\n{wm.for}\n{wm.ff.reader}
  (age<=modern) {wm.head}\n{wm.what} {wm.for}\n{wm.end}

# ---- the heading and the close (formulas) -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

wm.head (formula)
  Written into this life at {$home}, cycle {#year:digits}.
  A mark in the letters, made at {$home} in cycle {#year:digits}.
  For whoever reads living letters: {$home}, cycle {#year:digits}.
  Made at {$home}, {season.now}, cycle {#year:digits}.
  Cycle {#year:digits}. {$home}. This is our mark.
  (has:$home.quarter) {$home.quarter}, {$home}, cycle {#year:digits}: our mark.
  Our mark, set down at {$home} in the {nth} season of cycle {#year:digits}.

wm.end (formula)
  Here the mark ends; the life's own letters go on.
  End of the mark.
  That is all we wrote. The rest is its own.
  The mark ends here and begins again further on.
  Here our words stop and its work begins.

# ---- what the mark is ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

wm.what
  (3) {wm.part} {wm.does}, {wm.like}. {wm.short}
  (2) {wm.part} {wm.does}. {wm.sign}
  (2) {wm.sign} {wm.short}
wm.part
  This stretch of its letters
  This handful of words
  What you are reading
  This part of it
  This run of letters
  This short stretch of its code
  The stretch you have found
  This run of a few hundred letters
  What we wrote here
wm.does
  does nothing for the cell
  is copied each time it divides, and never read by it
  was set here by hand, a few letters a day
  is a letter, not a living thing
  says who made it, and in what cycle
  is the only part of it that talks
  costs it nothing to carry
  will be copied long after {wm.lab} is gone
  was the last of it to be written
  makes no {wm.thing}, and keeps no time
  was worked out on the {wm.surface} of {wm.lab} first
wm.thing
  wall
  food
  light
  poison
  colour
wm.surface
  long tables
  glass walls
  oldest machine
  night screens
wm.like
  like a name sewn into a coat
  as a potter presses a thumb into the clay
  the way a mason cuts a mark on the back of a stone
  like the seal on a letter
  like the maker's line under a song
  as a weaver works a colour into the edge of a cloth
  like a name scratched inside a ring
  as the {craft} workshops of {wm.place} mark what they make
  the way a keeper of the {herd} marks the young ones
  like the sign on a jar of {drink}
wm.short
  It is a signature.
  It repeats.
  It is ours.
  Read on: it comes again.
  We were here.
  (1)
wm.sign
  {wm.sign.it} {wm.sign.how}, {wm.sign.why}.
  {wm.sign.it} {wm.sign.how}; {wm.sign.hope}.
wm.sign.it
  Our signature
  The mark
  This signature of ours
  The mark we wrote
wm.sign.how
  comes round again every {wm.every} letters
  is written three letters to a sign of our script
  is spelt out in the old code our children learned
  sits where the cell will never read it
  repeats down the whole length of the life
  was written into every copy we grew
wm.sign.why
  so that the life would be known for ours wherever it spread
  so that nobody could say it had made itself
  in case {wm.lab} burned
  because the law of {wm.place} asked it of every made thing
  as every made thing of ours carries one
  for whoever comes after the {wm.harm}
  so that we could tell it from the wild
wm.sign.hope
  if it ever changes, the life has changed
  it will outlast {wm.lab}, and very likely us
  we counted on it lasting {wm.gens} generations without a fault
  somebody would read it one day, we thought
  nobody will see it who does not first take the life apart
wm.every
  few thousand
  ten thousand
  hundred thousand
  forty thousand
  million
wm.gens
  a thousand
  a hundred thousand
  a million
  ten million

# ---- who made it ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

wm.made
  {wm.who} {wm.did} {wm.at}{wm.when}.
  (2 has:writer) {wm.who} {wm.did} {wm.at}{wm.when}. {wm.mine}
wm.who
  {$me:name}
  {$me:name} and {wm.many}
  {$me:name}, with the help of {wm.many},
  {wm.many}, with {$me:name} at their head,
  {$me:name} and the rest of {wm.lab}
  {$me:name}, who did not live to see it spread,
wm.did
  made it
  wrote these words into it
  grew the first of it
  put it together, letter by letter,
  finished it
  set the mark
  spent {n} cycles on it
  tried it in the {fut.green} first and then made it
wm.at
  at {wm.lab} of {$home}
  in {wm.lab}
  under {mountain}
  in the glass rooms of the {fut.green}
  by {water}
  at {$home}, in the {fut.block}
  in the old rooms over {wm.place}
  at {wm.lab}, beside the {fut.gate}
wm.when
  , over {n} cycles
  , in the years of the {wm.harm}
  , after {festival}
  , in a single season
  , working nights
  , while {crop} was coming in
  , the year the {herd} died
  (1)
wm.mine
  We wrote the mark.
  We chose the words together.
  The mistakes are ours.
  We were young then.
  We hope it worked.
wm.many
  forty others
  the night shift
  {n} students
  the old ones who taught us
  a machine that did the counting
  half the school
  our families, who waited
  the {craft} workers of {wm.place}
wm.lab
  the gene house
  the long laboratory
  the living works
  the house of letters
  the {river} laboratory
  the school of the living
  the growing works
  the seed vault
  the work rooms over {wm.place}
  (has:mind) the halls of {mind}
  the glass rooms of the {fut.green}
wm.place
  {city}
  {city2}
  {$home}
  the {river} country
wm.harm
  dust
  long drought
  sickness
  poisoned rain
  great heat
  empty seas
  fevers
  failing harvests

# ---- a saying, and the reader -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

wm.say
  (3) {wm.say.lead} {proverb}.
  {$me:name} {wm.say.chose}: {proverb}.
  {wm.say.why}, so here is one of {wm.place}: {proverb}.
wm.say.lead
  As we say,
  Our grandmothers used to say that
  There is a saying at {$home}:
  As they say at {city2},
  At {festival} they still say that
  An old saying, for whoever reads this:
  The children of {wm.place} learn early that
  The keepers of the {herd} say that
  In the {craft} workshops they say that
  There is a saying painted on the old {fut.sys.n}:
  The {fut.block} have a saying of their own:
  {$me:name} used to say that
  A saying of the {river} country:
  They write it over the {fut.gate}:
  As the old songs of {festival} have it,
wm.say.chose
  asked for a saying to go in, and chose this one
  wanted a saying written in, and the others let it be this one
  argued for a long time over the saying, and chose this
  put in the saying the {craft} workers say
wm.say.why
  A mark should hold something besides names
  A cell will carry it for ever
  We had room for a few more words
  Every made thing should carry a saying

wm.reader
  (3) {wm.reader.who}: {wm.reader.short}
  (3) {wm.reader.alone} {wm.reader.short2}
  If you can read this, {wm.reader.then}{wm.reader.coda}. {wm.reader.short2}
wm.reader.who
  Reader
  To the reader
  To you
  Finder
  Whoever you are
wm.reader.short
  be kind to it.
  it is yours now.
  remember us.
  look after it.
  we were the {people}.
  goodbye.
  read it slowly.
  it did us no harm.
wm.reader.alone
  Be kind to it.
  It is yours now.
  Remember us.
  Look after it.
  We were the {people}.
  Goodbye.
  Read it slowly.
  It did us no harm.
wm.reader.short2
  We were here.
  We meant well.
  Thank you.
  It is ours, and yours.
  (1)
wm.reader.then
  you have learned our words
  you know more of us than our neighbours did
  you have taken our life apart, and we forgive you
  you have come a long way
  the {fut.green} must have done well
  you have read the {nth} copy of it, or the millionth
  you are one of very few
  something of ours has reached you
  the life has carried it farther than we hoped
wm.reader.coda
  , and we are glad
  , reader
  , and we thank you
  , whoever you are
  (2)
)VG"
